# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   M. Lebeda et al. (2026). Revealing interstitial energetics in Ti-23Nb-0.7Ta-2Zr gum metal base alloy via universal machine learning interatomic potentials.
#   Journal of Materials Research and Technology. doi:10.1016/j.jmrt.2026.02.204  arXiv:2512.05568v3
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2512.05568v3 (sha256 6cb8f2395e45c4d3...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 270 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/lebeda2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: three pretrained universal MLIPs (MACE-MATPES-PBE-0,
# Orb-v3, SevenNet-0) used for geometry optimisation of 6,750 interstitial
# configurations in three 250-atom SQS cells of the Ti-23Nb-0.7Ta-2Zr gum
# metal base alloy, with DFT checks of six O and six H configurations. The
# DFT comparisons are given only in figures (energy orderings and 4.2-4.8 eV
# energy differences for H), so no error metric is encoded.

