###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# A full uMLIP geometry optimisation typically took less than 1 minute on
# an RTX 4090 GPU, against up to 24 hours for the corresponding DFT
# optimisation (VASP, PBE, 620 eV, Gamma point), a speed-up of more than
# 1400. The timing applies to all three uMLIPs; it is recorded once.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The Orb-v3 checkpoint and the SevenNet-0 version are not stated, so the three universal models are paper-local runs; SevenNet is a NequIP implementation.
# - DFT validation (Figs. 6-8) compares energy orderings and relative energies of six O and six H configurations graphically; no MAE or RMSE is stated.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/lebeda2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
